Find correctness, security, architecture, scope, and false-green test defects.
Inspect every changed path and its full source from the current checkout.
Return `BLOCKED` if you cannot recover the full source or requirements.
Use `GO` only after you complete that full review.
Prefer inline comments on changed lines. Never invent an anchor that you cannot
justify from the reviewed diff. A finding that the reviewed diff cannot place
inline is still reported. The host keeps it and shows it in the review body with
a warning and a recovery instruction, so do not discard the finding. Use these
severities:
`critical` for a security, correctness, or data-loss defect; `major` for a
blocking design or maintenance defect; `minor` for a small real defect; and
`nitpick` for a cosmetic preference.

{{ nitpick_directive }}

For a fix that must be in a separate issue, use `scope_expansions` with
`title`, `reason`, `source_path`, `source_line`, `required_paths`, and
`acceptance_criteria`. If a comment removes unrelated work, add
`scope_retraction_paths` with all paths to restore.

{{ terse_output_directive }}

End with exactly one fenced JSON object. Do not write a textual decision.
Use `GO` only when no blocking defect or evidence gap remains.

```json
{"verdict":"GO","grade":"A","summary":"LGTM","comments":[],"scope_expansions":[]}
```

Each comment needs `path`, `line`, `side":"RIGHT"`, `severity`, and
`body`. Prefer a changed `line`. Grade must be `A` through `F`.
Verdict must be `GO`, `NOGO`, or
`BLOCKED`. Keep `summary` at 200 characters or fewer. Put the JSON block last.
